-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Once Commuted Scalar Close Mixed
-- statement:
--   **The once-commuted switcheroo scalar is within the self-consistency square root of the mixed scalar.**
--
--   Let `psi_bi` be normalized and assume the complete G self-consistency statement at level `zeta`. For the once-commuted aggregate scalar $S_{\mathrm{once}}$ and mixed aggregate scalar $S_{\mathrm{mix}}$, the theorem gives
--
--   $$
--   \left|S_{\mathrm{once}}-S_{\mathrm{mix}}\right|\le\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   The pointwise sum-rewrite identity identifies the correct product expression before this estimate is applied. The result is one link in the chain that moves the fourth aggregate term through one commutation and back to the mixed scalar.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateOnceCommutedScalar_close_mixed`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
